{
  "version": 1,
  "operation": "SdpaBackward",
  "description": "SDPA backward with Philox dropout (probability, INT64 seed and offset device tensors) AND padding (both seq_len tensors) over hipkernel:flydsl_sdpa_bwd_split. The harness draws the keep mask over the declared extents (SEM-015; padded and packed graphs follow the declared-extent layout, COVERAGE.md 9.3) and grades the engine against the explicit-mask gradient; a kernel that derives its Philox plane offsets from the live lengths instead disagrees with the oracle for every batch entry shorter than the declared extent. Otherwise as SdpaBackward/FlydslBwdSplitPadded (valid lengths max(1, Sq - i * pad_q) and max(1, Skv - i * pad_kv) for batch index i; masks none, top-left and bottom-right causal) and SdpaBackward/FlydslBwdSplitDropout.",
  "engine": "hipkernel:flydsl_sdpa_bwd_split",
  "template": "../../integration-test-bundles/quick/SdpaBackward/Default/graph.template.json",
